import Mathlib
import AssemblyP1.GenomeOrbitAdapter
import AssemblyP1.BayesOptimalityCertificate
import AssemblyP1.IidMapMonotonicity

/-!
# The dihedral (rotation + reverse-complement) orbit quotient (#269)

The merged orbit machinery (`AssemblyP1.GenomeOrbitAdapter`, PR #200) quotients
the finite circular oriented read model by **rotation** only, because the
oriented one-strand window pmf `p_G(w) = mult_G(w)/|G|` is automatically
rotation invariant.  Reverse complement is a *different* action: an oriented
one-strand read distribution need not be RC invariant, and the merged adapter
explicitly declines to claim an RC quotient.

This module closes that gap, conditionally and honestly.

## The dihedral quotient

Fix a finite read alphabet `α`, a base complement involution `c : α → α`
(`c (c a) = a`), and a positive circular genome length `G`.  The reverse
complement of a circular word is

    rcWord c S = fun i => c (S (-i)).

It conjugates rotation to inverse rotation
(`rcWord_rotWord`), is an involution (`rcWord_involutive`), and therefore acts
on the rotation-orbit type as an involution `rcOrbit`
(`rcOrbit_involutive`).  The **dihedral equivalence** on rotation classes
identifies a class with its reverse complement; it is the two-element
equivalence relation `rcSetoid` generated by `rcOrbit`.  Its quotient
`Quotient (rcSetoid c hc)` is the finite dihedral orbit quotient.

## The RC-invariance hypothesis

A rotation-invariant read score `p` descends to the dihedral quotient exactly
when it is also RC invariant, `∀ S, p (rcWord c S) = p S` (`dihedralScore`).
For the raw oriented circular read pmf this is the hypothesis `RCInvariant c`.
It is a **genuine extra hypothesis**, not a consequence of the model: the
length-3 genome `001` over `{0,1}` has `p(00) = 1/3` while its reverse
complement has `p(00) = 0`, so the raw read pmf does **not** descend to dihedral
classes (`Obstruction.readPmf_not_rcInvariant`,
`Obstruction.no_dihedral_descent`).  This is the precise obstruction that makes
the conditional statement the correct one.

The hypothesis is nevertheless satisfiable nondegenerately: the
**strand-symmetrized** read law `symReadPmf c S w = (p_S(w) + p_{rc(S)}(w))/2`
(a double-stranded molecule whose sequenced strand is chosen uniformly at
random) is automatically rotation- and RC-invariant, so it descends to the
dihedral quotient unconditionally.

## What is proved (all kernel-checked, no `sorry`/`admit`/new axiom)

* `dihedral_map_success_monotone` — prior-averaged zero-one success of the
  constructed MAP policy is nondecreasing in the number of reads `n` (including
  `n = 0`) for any prior on dihedral classes.
* `uniform_dihedral_prior_ML` — under the **uniform** prior on dihedral classes
  the MAP policy is exactly a maximum-likelihood policy.
* `dihedral_certificate` — a policy is Bayes-optimal iff it is pointwise MAP.
* `dihedral_tie_all_optimal` — explicit tie handling: when the dihedral joint is
  class-independent every constant policy is optimal, so MAP is non-unique.
* `readPmf_*` — the above for the raw oriented read pmf under `RCInvariant`.
* `sym_*` — the above unconditionally for the strand-symmetrized model.

This is prior-averaged success for a fixed finite observation model.  It is not
a per-true-genome claim (the merged
`GenomeOrbitAdapter.PerTruthDrop.perTruth_true_drops` refutes per-truth
monotonicity), not a global "ML is best" claim, not the MB09 fixed-`N`
product-binomial pseudo-likelihood, not the §6.2 feasible-flow optimization,
and not the truth-dependent event-conditional inference of #266.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace AssemblyP1.DihedralOrbitQuotient

open Finset BigOperators

variable {α : Type*} [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]

/-! ## 1. Reverse complement on circular words -/

/-- Reverse complement of a circular word under a base complement `c`:
`(rcWord c S) i = c (S (-i))`. -/
def rcWord (c : α → α) {G : ℕ} (S : ZMod G → α) : ZMod G → α :=
  fun i => c (S (-i))

section RC

variable {G : ℕ} [NeZero G]

omit [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] in
/-- Reverse complement conjugates a rotation to the inverse rotation. -/
theorem rcWord_rotWord (c : α → α) (S : ZMod G → α) (j : ZMod G) :
    rcWord c (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) =
      GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord (rcWord c S) (-j) := by
  funext i
  simp only [rcWord, GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord]
  congr 1
  abel

omit [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] in
/-- Reverse complement is an involution when the base complement is. -/
theorem rcWord_involutive (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (S : ZMod G → α) : rcWord c (rcWord c S) = S := by
  funext i
  simpa only [rcWord, neg_neg] using hc (S i)

/-- Reverse complement acts on rotation-orbit classes. -/
noncomputable def rcOrbit (c : α → α) (_hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G) →
      Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G) :=
  Quotient.lift (fun S => Quotient.mk _ (rcWord c S)) (by
    intro S T h
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := h
    rw [rcWord_rotWord]
    exact Quotient.sound ⟨-j, rfl⟩)

/-- Reverse complement is an involution on rotation-orbit classes. -/
theorem rcOrbit_involutive (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Function.Involutive (rcOrbit (α := α) (G := G) c hc) := by
  intro o
  refine Quotient.inductionOn o ?_
  intro S
  simp only [rcOrbit, Quotient.lift_mk, rcWord_involutive c hc]

/-- Dihedral equivalence on rotation classes: identify a class with its reverse
complement. -/
def rcSetoid (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Setoid (Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G)) where
  r o o' := o' = o ∨ o' = rcOrbit (G := G) c hc o
  iseqv := by
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · intro o
      exact Or.inl rfl
    · intro o o' h
      rcases h with h | h
      · exact Or.inl h.symm
      · exact Or.inr (by rw [h, rcOrbit_involutive (G := G) c hc o])
    · intro o o' o'' h1 h2
      rcases h1 with h1 | h1 <;> rcases h2 with h2 | h2
      · exact Or.inl (h2.trans h1)
      · exact Or.inr (by rw [h2, h1])
      · exact Or.inr (h2.trans h1)
      · exact Or.inl (by rw [h2, h1, rcOrbit_involutive (G := G) c hc o])

/-- Decidable equality on the dihedral quotient (classical, used only to state
and prove the decision-theoretic theorems). -/
noncomputable instance instDecidableEqQuotientRcSetoid (c : α → α)
    (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    DecidableEq (Quotient (rcSetoid (α := α) (G := G) c hc)) :=
  Classical.decEq _

/-- The dihedral quotient is finite. -/
noncomputable instance instFintypeQuotientRcSetoid (c : α → α)
    (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Fintype (Quotient (rcSetoid (α := α) (G := G) c hc)) := by
  classical
  exact Quotient.fintype _

/-- The dihedral quotient is nonempty whenever the read alphabet is. -/
instance instNonemptyQuotientRcSetoid [Nonempty α] (c : α → α)
    (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Nonempty (Quotient (rcSetoid (α := α) (G := G) c hc)) :=
  ⟨Quotient.mk _
    (Classical.choice (inferInstance : Nonempty (Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G))))⟩

end RC

/-! ## 2. Descent of a read score to rotation and dihedral orbits -/

section Score

variable {G L : ℕ} [NeZero G]

/-- A read score constant on rotation orbits descends to the rotation-orbit
type. -/
noncomputable def orbitScore (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S) :
    Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ :=
  Quotient.lift p (by
    intro S T h
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := h
    exact (hrot S j).symm)

/-- A rotation-invariant score that is also reverse-complement invariant is
constant on dihedral classes. -/
theorem orbitScore_rcOrbit (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (o : Quotient (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid α G)) :
    orbitScore (G := G) (L := L) p hrot (rcOrbit (G := G) c hc o) =
      orbitScore (G := G) (L := L) p hrot o := by
  refine Quotient.inductionOn o ?_
  intro S
  simp only [rcOrbit, Quotient.lift_mk, orbitScore]
  exact hRC S

/-- A rotation- and reverse-complement-invariant score descends to the dihedral
orbit quotient. -/
noncomputable def dihedralScore (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S) :
    Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ :=
  Quotient.lift (orbitScore (G := G) (L := L) p hrot) (by
    intro o o' h
    rcases h with h | h
    · rw [h]
    · rw [h, orbitScore_rcOrbit (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC o])

/-- A normalized score stays normalized after descending to the dihedral
quotient. -/
theorem dihedralScore_sum_one (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (hnorm : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, ∑ w : Fin L → α, p S w = 1)
    (d : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    ∑ w : Fin L → α, dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC d w = 1 := by
  refine Quotient.inductionOn d ?_
  intro o
  refine Quotient.inductionOn o ?_
  intro S
  simp only [dihedralScore, orbitScore]
  exact hnorm S

/-! ## 3. MAP/ML optimality on the dihedral quotient -/

/-- **Dihedral prior-averaged success monotonicity.**  For the exact finite iid
read model on dihedral orbit classes, the constructed MAP policy's
prior-averaged zero-one success does not decrease when one more read is
observed, for every `n` including `0` and for an arbitrary prior on dihedral
classes. -/
theorem dihedral_map_success_monotone [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (hnorm : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, ∑ w : Fin L → α, p S w = 1)
    (π : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ) (n : ℕ) :
    IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccess π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n ≤
      IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccessSucc π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n :=
  IidMapMonotonicity.iid_map_success_monotone π
    (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n
    (fun d => dihedralScore_sum_one (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC hnorm d)

/-- Uniform prior on dihedral orbit classes. -/
noncomputable def uniformDihedralPrior (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ :=
  fun _ => 1 / (Fintype.card (Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) : ℝ)

/-- The uniform dihedral prior is a probability distribution. -/
theorem uniformDihedralPrior_sum_one [Nonempty α] (c : α → α)
    (hc : Function.Involutive c) :
    ∑ o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc),
        uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc o = 1 := by
  classical
  have hcard : (Fintype.card (Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by
    exact_mod_cast Fintype.card_ne_zero
  unfold uniformDihedralPrior
  rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul]
  rw [mul_one_div, div_self hcard]

/-- Exact dihedral iid likelihood of the sample `x` under class `o`. -/
noncomputable def dihedralLikelihood (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (n : ℕ) (o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc))
    (x : Fin n → (Fin L → α)) : ℝ :=
  ∏ i : Fin n, dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC o (x i)

/-- **Uniform dihedral prior implies MAP = ML.**  Under the uniform prior on
dihedral orbit classes, the constructed MAP policy's decision maximizes the
exact iid likelihood pointwise. -/
theorem uniform_dihedral_prior_ML [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → (Fin L → α))
    (o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC n o x ≤
      dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC n
        (FiniteBayesDecision.chooseMAP
          (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
            (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n) x) x := by
  classical
  have hcard : 0 < (Fintype.card (Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) : ℝ) :=
    Nat.cast_pos.mpr (Fintype.card_pos_iff.mpr inferInstance)
  have hpos : 0 < uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc o := by
    unfold uniformDihedralPrior
    exact one_div_pos.mpr hcard
  have hmax := FiniteBayesDecision.chooseMAP_maximizes
    (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
      (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n) x o
  simp only [IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint, dihedralLikelihood] at hmax ⊢
  exact le_of_mul_le_mul_left hmax hpos

/-- **The dihedral optimality certificate.**  A policy on dihedral classes is
Bayes-optimal exactly when it is pointwise MAP for the exact iid dihedral joint,
for every sample size `n` including `0`. -/
theorem dihedral_certificate [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (π : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ) (n : ℕ)
    (d : (Fin n → (Fin L → α)) → Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    BayesOptimalityCertificate.BayesOptimal
        (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint π
          (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n) d ↔
      BayesOptimalityCertificate.PointwiseMAP
        (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint π
          (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n) d :=
  BayesOptimalityCertificate.pointwiseMAP_iff_bayesOptimal _ d

/-- **Explicit tie handling.**  If the dihedral iid joint is independent of the
class at every sample, then *every* constant policy is Bayes-optimal, so the MAP
is non-unique whenever the dihedral quotient has at least two classes. -/
theorem dihedral_tie_all_optimal [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (p : (ZMod G → α) → (Fin L → α) → ℝ)
    (hrot : ∀ S (j : ZMod G), p (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) = p S)
    (hRC : ∀ S : ZMod G → α, p (rcWord c S) = p S)
    (n : ℕ)
    (hconst : ∀ o o' (x : Fin n → (Fin L → α)),
      IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n o x =
      IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n o' x) :
    ∀ o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc),
      BayesOptimalityCertificate.BayesOptimal
        (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
          (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc p hrot hRC) n) (fun _ => o) := by
  intro o
  apply BayesOptimalityCertificate.pointwiseMAP_imp_bayesOptimal
  intro x θ
  rw [hconst θ o x]

end Score

/-! ## 4. The raw oriented read model under RC-invariance -/

section ReadPmf

variable {G L : ℕ} [NeZero G]

/-- The RC-invariance hypothesis on the raw oriented circular read pmf: reverse
complement does not change the window pmf.  This is a genuine extra hypothesis;
section 6 exhibits a concrete failure. -/
def RCInvariant (c : α → α) : Prop :=
  ∀ S : ZMod G → α,
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L) (rcWord c S) =
      GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L) S

/-- The raw read pmf is rotation invariant, as a function equality. -/
theorem readPmf_rotInvariant (S : ZMod G → α) (j : ZMod G) :
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L)
        (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) =
      GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L) S :=
  funext fun w => GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_rotWord S j w

/-- **Dihedral prior-averaged success monotonicity for the raw read model under
RC-invariance.** -/
theorem readPmf_dihedral_map_success_monotone [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (hRC : RCInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c)
    (π : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ) (n : ℕ) :
    IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccess π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc
          (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
          (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC) n ≤
      IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccessSucc π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc
          (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
          (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC) n :=
  dihedral_map_success_monotone (G := G) (L := L) c hc
    (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
    (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC
    (fun S => GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_sum_one S) π n

/-- **Uniform dihedral prior implies MAP = ML for the raw read model under
RC-invariance.** -/
theorem readPmf_uniform_dihedral_prior_ML [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (hRC : RCInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c)
    (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → (Fin L → α))
    (o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc
        (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
        (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC n o x ≤
      dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc
        (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
        (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC n
        (FiniteBayesDecision.chooseMAP
          (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
            (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc
              (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
              (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC) n)
          x) x :=
  uniform_dihedral_prior_ML (G := G) (L := L) c hc
    (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
    (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC n x o

/-- **The dihedral optimality certificate for the raw read model under
RC-invariance.** -/
theorem readPmf_dihedral_certificate [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (hRC : RCInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c)
    (π : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ) (n : ℕ)
    (d : (Fin n → (Fin L → α)) → Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    BayesOptimalityCertificate.BayesOptimal
        (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint π
          (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc
            (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
            (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC) n) d ↔
      BayesOptimalityCertificate.PointwiseMAP
        (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint π
          (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc
            (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
            (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC) n) d :=
  dihedral_certificate (G := G) (L := L) c hc
    (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L))
    (fun S j => readPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) S j) hRC π n d

end ReadPmf

/-! ## 5. A concrete RC-invariant model: strand-symmetrized reads -/

section Symmetrized

variable {G L : ℕ} [NeZero G]

/-- Strand-symmetrized read pmf: the average of the forward-strand and
reverse-complement-strand window pmfs, modelling a double-stranded molecule
whose sequenced strand is chosen uniformly at random. -/
noncomputable def symReadPmf (c : α → α) (S : ZMod G → α) (w : Fin L → α) : ℝ :=
  (GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L) S w +
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := G) (L := L) (rcWord c S) w) / 2

/-- The strand-symmetrized read pmf is rotation invariant. -/
theorem symReadPmf_rotInvariant (c : α → α) (S : ZMod G → α) (j : ZMod G) :
    symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotWord S j) =
      symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c S := by
  funext w
  unfold symReadPmf
  rw [GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_rotWord S j w, rcWord_rotWord,
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_rotWord (rcWord c S) (-j) w]

/-- The strand-symmetrized read pmf is reverse-complement invariant. -/
theorem symReadPmf_rcInvariant (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (S : ZMod G → α) :
    symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c (rcWord c S) =
      symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c S := by
  funext w
  unfold symReadPmf
  rw [rcWord_involutive c hc S]
  ring

/-- The strand-symmetrized read pmf is normalized. -/
theorem symReadPmf_sum_one (c : α → α) (S : ZMod G → α) :
    ∑ w : Fin L → α, symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c S w = 1 := by
  unfold symReadPmf
  rw [← Finset.sum_div, Finset.sum_add_distrib,
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_sum_one S,
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf_sum_one (rcWord c S)]
  norm_num

/-- **Unconditional dihedral prior-averaged success monotonicity for the
strand-symmetrized model.** -/
theorem sym_dihedral_map_success_monotone [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (π : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc) → ℝ) (n : ℕ) :
    IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccess π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
          (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j) (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S)) n ≤
      IidMapMonotonicity.mapSuccessSucc π
        (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
          (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j) (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S)) n :=
  dihedral_map_success_monotone (G := G) (L := L) c hc
    (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
    (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j)
    (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S)
    (fun S => symReadPmf_sum_one (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S) π n

/-- **Unconditional uniform-dihedral-prior MAP = ML for the strand-symmetrized
model.** -/
theorem sym_uniform_dihedral_prior_ML [Nonempty α]
    (c : α → α) (hc : Function.Involutive c)
    (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → (Fin L → α))
    (o : Quotient (rcSetoid (G := G) c hc)) :
    dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
        (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j)
        (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S) n o x ≤
      dihedralLikelihood (G := G) (L := L) c hc (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
        (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j)
        (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S) n
        (FiniteBayesDecision.chooseMAP
          (IidMapMonotonicity.iidJoint (uniformDihedralPrior (G := G) c hc)
            (dihedralScore (G := G) (L := L) c hc (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
              (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j) (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S))
            n) x) x :=
  uniform_dihedral_prior_ML (G := G) (L := L) c hc
    (symReadPmf (G := G) (L := L) c)
    (fun S j => symReadPmf_rotInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c S j)
    (fun S => symReadPmf_rcInvariant (α := α) (G := G) (L := L) c hc S) n x o

end Symmetrized

/-! ## 6. The RC-invariance hypothesis is not automatic (precise obstruction) -/

namespace Obstruction

/-- The two-symbol DNA complement: swap `0` and `1`. -/
def comp2 : Fin 2 → Fin 2 := fun i => if i = 0 then 1 else 0

/-- `comp2` is an involution. -/
theorem comp2_involutive : Function.Involutive comp2 := by
  intro i
  fin_cases i <;> rfl

/-- The length-3 circular genome `0 0 1` over the two-symbol alphabet. -/
def S3 : ZMod 3 → Fin 2 := fun i => if i = (2 : ZMod 3) then 1 else 0

/-- The all-zero length-2 read word. -/
def w00 : Fin 2 → Fin 2 := fun _ => 0

/-- The genome `001` spells `00` at exactly one start. -/
theorem mult_S3_w00 : GenomeOrbitAdapter.mult (G := 3) (L := 2) S3 w00 = 1 := by
  decide

/-- Its reverse complement spells `00` at no start. -/
theorem mult_rcS3_w00 :
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.mult (G := 3) (L := 2) (rcWord comp2 S3) w00 = 0 := by
  decide

/-- So `p_{001}(00) = 1/3`. -/
theorem readPmf_S3_w00 :
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := 3) (L := 2) S3 w00 = 1 / 3 := by
  unfold GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf
  rw [mult_S3_w00]
  norm_num

/-- while `p_{rc(001)}(00) = 0`. -/
theorem readPmf_rcS3_w00 :
    GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := 3) (L := 2) (rcWord comp2 S3) w00 = 0 := by
  unfold GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf
  rw [mult_rcS3_w00]
  norm_num

/-- **The raw oriented read pmf is not RC invariant.**  This kernel-checked
counterexample shows the `RCInvariant` hypothesis is a genuine constraint on the
raw one-strand circular read model. -/
theorem readPmf_not_rcInvariant :
    ¬ RCInvariant (α := Fin 2) (G := 3) (L := 2) comp2 := by
  intro h
  have hw := congrFun (h S3) w00
  rw [readPmf_S3_w00, readPmf_rcS3_w00] at hw
  norm_num at hw

/-- **No dihedral descent for the raw oriented read model.**  There is no
function on the dihedral orbit quotient whose pullback is the raw oriented read
pmf: if there were, the RC-related genomes `001` and its reverse complement
would have the same pmf, contradicting `readPmf_not_rcInvariant`. -/
theorem no_dihedral_descent :
    ¬ ∃ g : Quotient (rcSetoid (α := Fin 2) (G := 3) comp2 comp2_involutive) →
          (Fin 2 → Fin 2) → ℝ,
        ∀ S : ZMod 3 → Fin 2,
          g (Quotient.mk _ (Quotient.mk _ S)) =
            GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := 3) (L := 2) S := by
  rintro ⟨g, hg⟩
  have hrel : (rcSetoid (α := Fin 2) (G := 3) comp2 comp2_involutive).r
      (Quotient.mk (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid (Fin 2) 3) S3)
      (Quotient.mk (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid (Fin 2) 3) (rcWord comp2 S3)) :=
    Or.inr (by simp [rcOrbit])
  have heq :
      Quotient.mk (rcSetoid (α := Fin 2) (G := 3) comp2 comp2_involutive)
          (Quotient.mk (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid (Fin 2) 3) S3) =
        Quotient.mk (rcSetoid (α := Fin 2) (G := 3) comp2 comp2_involutive)
          (Quotient.mk (GenomeOrbitAdapter.rotSetoid (Fin 2) 3) (rcWord comp2 S3)) :=
    Quotient.sound hrel
  have hfun : GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := 3) (L := 2) S3 =
      GenomeOrbitAdapter.readPmf (G := 3) (L := 2) (rcWord comp2 S3) := by
    rw [← hg S3, ← hg (rcWord comp2 S3), heq]
  have hw := congrFun hfun w00
  rw [readPmf_S3_w00, readPmf_rcS3_w00] at hw
  norm_num at hw

end Obstruction

